12838	{"artifactId":"LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:16:37.665Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s1 acceptance criterion (ac1-ac6 of DEF §6.1) is designed: one item per story with all evidence, s1/S001 joined with sourceIds kept, ambiguity notices instead of merging, fix stories as distinct children of an issue, unresolved-parent notice plus no invented epic, tasks identified through their parent story.","evidence":"DEF.md lines 118-123 list ac1-ac6. The LLD's §3.2 construction rules (groups, standalone precedence, EXT membership, fix stories by shared hash, correctsRef resolution, task minting via taskWorkflowId) and §3.3 notice rules cover each one. Non-goals are respected: no route, gate or currency logic is designed, and the adjacent-scope list pushes those to s2-s5. [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The id minters throw on an invalid createdAt or a non-hex hash, and safeCanonical turns any throw into undefined (id.ts:91-106, :185), so the H-form fallback can never throw.","evidence":"id.ts:91-94 `if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) throw`; :104 `if (... !/^[0-9a-f]{8,}$/.test(epicHash)) throw`; :185-186 `try { return toCanonical(mint()); } catch { return undefined; }`. storyIdToOrdinal (:123-124) also throws on 'x', and safeCanonical catches that too. [files: src/workflow/id.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"buildRecordFolderArgs anchors a standalone story on the LLD's epicCreatedAt, then the LLD's createdAt, then the definition head's createdAt, then the record's own createdAt; an epic story anchors on the DEF/ISSUE createdAt. The builder's anchor order copies this.","evidence":"storage.ts:420-421 `createdAtISO: (standalone ? readEpicCreatedAtStamp(repoPath, lldArtifactId(...)) : undefined) ?? upstream.createdAt ?? head.createdAt ?? ownCreatedAt`, where upstream is the LLD core for standalone (:385-387) and readEpicDefinitionCore (DEF then ISSUE, :357-365) for epic. Confirmed against real folders: LLD-761a43a6fa645815-s9 has createdAt 2026-08-05 but its folder is E20260803761a43a6, which is the DEF's date. LLD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1 (2026-08-04, no head) has folder E20260804d88062a6. The trivial BUILD-d5a433047dc3439f-s1 (2026-09-30) has folder E20260930d5a43304. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"BUILD records can carry a standalone flag that disagrees with the head/LLD, so BUILD standalone must be ignored when a head or LLD exists; inheritedStoryStandalone takes the head first, then the LLD.","evidence":"storage.ts:252-261 `readEpicDefinitionCore(...).standalone ?? readArtifactCore(..., lldArtifactId(...)).standalone ?? fallback`. Store: BUILD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1 has `\"standalone\": false` while LLD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1 has `\"standalone\": true`. Same for the dfc0371b7200f5b5 S001 pair. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"workflow.pending reads approval as non-empty meta.approvedAt / meta.rejectedAt, the stamps gates.ts writes, and mints its per-record id from epicCreatedAt ?? createdAt (a known divergence the design does not test against).","evidence":"pending.ts:126-128 checks `meta['approvedAt']` / `meta['rejectedAt']` as non-empty strings; gates.ts:606 `const approvedAt = new Date().toISOString();` and :954 `const rejectedAt = ...`. pending.ts:161-170 `const createdAt = str(meta['epicCreatedAt']) ?? str(meta['createdAt'])`. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No existing helper already reads the whole artifact store into records, so loadArtifactRecordSet is genuinely new; the reused id.ts minters and storage.ts helpers exist with the signatures the LLD states.","evidence":"The only readdirSync over ARTIFACTS_DIR outside tests is pending.ts's kind-filtered listing, which drops records that aren't pending. In tests it appears only in define-extend-e2e, resolve-comment and artifact-content. Signatures exist as stated: id.ts exports epicWorkflowId(hash, createdAt), storyWorkflowId(hash, createdAt, storyId), taskWorkflowId(..., taskId), toCanonical, safeCanonical, parseWorkflowId, taskIdToOrdinal and deriveWorkItemIdentity; storage.ts:181 exports workItemAnchorCreatedAt(meta). [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed call sites (id.ts minters/parsers, storage.ts ARTIFACTS_DIR and workItemAnchorCreatedAt) cover everything the new module consumes, and no existing caller has to change because the module is additive under src/workflow/delivery/.","evidence":"src/workflow/delivery/ does not exist yet (glob is empty), so no existing signature changes. Every external symbol the LLD's construction rules name is in its call-site lists and exists. inheritedStoryStandalone and buildRecordFolderArgs are deliberately re-implemented in memory rather than called, because both read the disk (storage.ts:300-318, 373-425), and the LLD says so explicitly. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"AMD records are flat, with top-level epicHash, amendment, proposedAt, status and an optional approvedAt; every other kind is { meta, body }.","evidence":"AMD-761a43a6fa645815-1.json has top-level `\"id\"`, `\"epicHash\"`, `\"amendment\": {...}`, `\"proposedAt\"`, `\"status\": \"approved\"`, `\"approvedAt\"`. The pending AMDs (e.g. AMD-edb76e2e4d41217d-2) have `status: pending` and no approvedAt. CR-d5a433047dc3439f-s1 has meta.epicHash and meta.storyId inside `meta`. EXT records keep meta.approvedAt inside meta (EXT-761a43a6fa645815-s9.json:97), with body.addedStory {id,title} and body.amendmentId. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-761a43a6fa645815-1.json, .insrc/artifacts/EXT-761a43a6fa645815-s9.json, .insrc/artifacts/CR-d5a433047dc3439f-s1.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Work-item hashes come from meta.issueHash for an ISSUE and meta.specHash for a SPEC, a DEF's meta.seededFromSpec holds the bare SPEC hash, and ISSUE titles are in body.title.","evidence":"ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72.json:20 `\"issueHash\": \"0855311b6b32eb72\"`; SPEC-*.json:20 `\"specHash\": ...`; DEF-914cbf5ea9026b92.json:22 `\"seededFromSpec\": \"26c321a52f39c4b7\"`, which matches SPEC-26c321a52f39c4b7. All 44 ISSUE files carry a `title` field at body depth. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72.json, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-914cbf5ea9026b92.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.3","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older records mix story-id forms (s1, S001, s001) and story-level BUILD task ids (S001), and the loader and builder handle all of them without merging wrongly or creating spurious tasks.","evidence":"PLAN-dfc0371b7200f5b5-s1.json has `\"storyId\": \"s001\"`, while LLD, BUILD and CR use `S001`. storyIdToOrdinal's /^[sS](\\d+)$/ maps both to 1. Exactly 20 BUILD files contain a task `\"id\": \"S<n>\"` (e.g. BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1), matching c8; the LLD creates no task for these. No meta.storyId in the store is outside the s/S+digits form, so the ':R(<raw>)' path is defensive only. [files: .insrc/artifacts/PLAN-dfc0371b7200f5b5-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD implements only sc1-sc3, the contracts s1 owns, and leaves route (sc4), review/attention (sc5), currency/amendment staleness (sc6) and the snapshot/handler (sc7) to s2-s5. Its sc2 refinements (LLD-first anchor for standalone stories, and the H-form also covering an un-mintable createdAt or hash) stay inside s1's own contract.","evidence":"HLD.md:44, :92 and :141 name s1 as Owner Story for sc1, sc2 and sc3. The HLD's sc2 comment (:104-110) requires ids to equal the existing path-scheme folder, and the LLD's anchor refinement is what storage.ts:420-421 actually does. The notice table matches HLD:172-175 exactly (true for record-unreadable, identity-ambiguous, unresolved-parent, validation-conflict). No sc4-sc7 field or rule is designed. [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/HLD.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Slug-based parentRef resolution (against other work items' meta.epicSlug, excluding the issue's own hash) gives the stated outcome for every real parentRef shape: a self-slug gives null, an outward slug resolves, a bare hash resolves, and nothing in the store triggers false ambiguity.","evidence":"ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72 parentRef.slug 'bug-build-record-triage-routed-small' equals its own epicSlug, so it is excluded by hash and gives null. 'vs-code-editor-dev-chat-ui' appears only under hash f9563bf5bbb29c43, and 'add-daemon-driven-code-review-stage' only under 761a43a6fa645815 (the DEF plus LLD/PLAN/EXT/AMD records). 'artifact-docs-folders-fork-per-stage', referenced by ISSUE-0b2faed8 and ISSUE-3a98d279, appears only as the epicSlug of ISSUE-e20235c17f083a16 and so resolves uniquely. ISSUE-095906bac5bbacaf uses the bare hash 'd5a433047dc3439f' with storyId 's1', which matches the trivial BUILD/CR work item. Each failure (unreadable store, unreadable, invalid or meta-less file, unknown prefix, unparseable storyId, un-mintable anchor) has stated detection and handling in §5. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-095906bac5bbacaf.json, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3a98d27994547262.json, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-e20235c17f083a16.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of s1 ac1-ac6 maps to at least one named test over fabricated or real-shape records, and the real-shape fixtures the tests cite exist with the shapes the tests assume.","evidence":"§6's acceptance mapping lists tests for ac1-ac6. The fixtures it cites match the store: LLD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1 (standalone true, no head, no epicCreatedAt), BUILD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1 (standalone false), BUILD-d5a433047dc3439f-s1 (standalone true, sizeClass 'trivial', no head), ISSUE-57446545909fe95c (parentRef slug plus storyId 's1'), ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72 (self-slug), BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1 (S001 task id). One small wording issue: §6 calls the dfc0371b S001/s001 pair 'in epic dfc0371b', but that work item has no DEF and is standalone. The fixture still exercises the s1/S001 join. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-dfc0371b7200f5b5-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/PLAN-dfc0371b7200f5b5-s1.json]","action":"Optional: call the dfc0371b fixture a standalone work item rather than an epic in the test names.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-07T09:16:37.665Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
